The attached image (Figure 6) demonstrates how Nano-11 improves antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells and enhances antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest CD86 expression among OVA-positive myeloid cells in the draining lymph node, indicating their strong activation potential. Panel B further characterizes these OVA+ MigDCs from Nano-11 formulations as predominantly CD11b+Ly6C- cells. Panel C illustrates that Nano-11 (N11), similar to aluminum hydroxide (AH), significantly prolongs the retention of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) at the injection site over several days compared to soluble OVA, which dissipates rapidly.